## 1. Introduction
TechWave Inc. is a leading software development company located in San Francisco, California, specializing in artificial intelligence and machine learning solutions. As of October 2023, we employ 250 full-time staff members, and our workforce is expected to grow by 20% in the next fiscal year. This document outlines our hiring, training, benefits, and performance management strategies to attract, retain, and develop top talent.

## 2. Hiring Process

### 2.1 Job Posting
Job openings will be posted on multiple platforms, including:
- LinkedIn
- Indeed
- Glassdoor
- TechWave's Careers Page

| Position Title        | Date Posted | Closing Date | Department         |
|-----------------------|-------------|--------------|---------------------|
| Software Engineer      | Oct 1, 2023| Oct 31, 2023 | Development          |
| Data Scientist         | Oct 5, 2023| Nov 5, 2023  | Data Analytics       |
| UX/UI Designer         | Oct 10, 2023| Nov 10, 2023 | Product Design       |

### 2.2 Candidate Screening
All applications will be reviewed by the HR team, led by Sarah Johnson, utilizing an Applicant Tracking System (ATS) known as "HirePro." Resumes will be screened based on the following criteria:
- Relevant experience
- Skills match
- Educational background

### 2.3 Interview Process
Shortlisted candidates will undergo a multi-stage interview process:
1. **Initial Screening:** Conducted by HR (Sarah Johnson and Lisa Patel, HR Specialist).
2. **Technical Interview:** Conducted by the hiring manager (Mark Thompson, Head of Development) and a senior team member.
3. **Final Interview:** Conducted by Robert Mills (COO) and Lisa Chen (CEO).

### 2.4 Offer and Onboarding
Successful candidates will receive an offer letter generated via DocuSign and will be required to complete onboarding tasks via the "OnboardTech" system. The onboarding process includes:
- Completion of tax forms
- Acceptance of company policies
- Setup of health benefits

## 3. Training and Development

### 3.1 Orientation Program
New hires will participate in a comprehensive orientation program on their first day, facilitated by Sarah Johnson and Lisa Patel. The program includes:
- Welcome session about TechWave's culture and values
- Overview of company policies and procedures
- Introduction to team members

