## 4. Benefits

### 4.1 Compensation Structure
TechWave offers a competitive salary structure benchmarked against industry standards. The following table outlines the salary ranges for key positions:

| Position Title        | Minimum Salary | Maximum Salary | Average Salary |
|-----------------------|----------------|----------------|-----------------|
| Software Engineer      | $90,000        | $130,000       | $110,000        |
| Data Scientist         | $95,000        | $140,000       | $115,000        |
| UX/UI Designer         | $85,000        | $120,000       | $100,000        |

### 4.2 Health and Wellness Programs
TechWave believes in employee well-being and offers the following health benefits:
- Comprehensive health insurance plans through United Healthcare
- Annual health screenings
- Wellness incentives, including gym memberships and fitness challenges

### 4.3 Retirement Plans
Employees are eligible for a 401(k) plan after one year of service, with a company match up to 4%. Information sessions regarding retirement planning will be held bi-annually.

## 5. Performance Management

### 5.1 Evaluation Process
Performance evaluations are conducted bi-annually, with the next review cycle scheduled for December 2023 and June 2024. The evaluation process includes:
- Self-assessment by employees
- Peer reviews
- Manager assessments

### 5.2 Feedback Mechanisms
Continuous feedback is encouraged through:
- Monthly one-on-one meetings between employees and supervisors
- Anonymous employee surveys conducted via SurveyMonkey

### 5.3 Performance Improvement Plans
For employees underperforming, a structured Performance Improvement Plan (PIP) will be implemented. This plan includes:
- Clear performance goals
- A timeline for improvement (typically 30-60 days)
- Regular check-ins with HR and direct supervisors

